im Moore (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Tim Moore, a first-term Republican incumbent in a district drawn with an R+8 partisan lean, faces Democrat Lakesha Womack in the general election. Moore has raised over $1.5 million and holds $1.58 million on hand, while Womack has raised under $25,000 and shows negative cash on hand. No outside groups are opposing Moore, and the only public poll, a Republican-sponsored March survey of likely voters, showed him ahead by eight points.\n\nAll nine expert ratings favor Republicans, with several calling the race Solid or Safe R, and prediction markets give Womack roughly a one-in-seven chance. Moore has spent the fall touting FEMA funding for Helene recovery and bipartisan legislation. The race appears settled barring an unexpected late shift in the national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0543, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -11.0}]}